The other posters have given good advice regarding wizards in general.
But remember that wizards have a relatively high base chance of writing
unknown spellbooks. If I start with a magic marker, I blank the
spellbooks and write identify (in the guaranteed blessed one) and light
(in the other one). Light is very useful in its own right, and it trains
Divination skill for identify. But even if you do not suceed writing
light and thus do not have a means of easy training (if you do not start
with detect monsters/food), you can still cast identify; even at 85%
failure rate, it is a blessing. 

Some players see this as gambling, but really, what you are risking
(besides the two dips) is just the first charge of an /optional/ starting
item.

